## Harness: Feature Development

For any feature, bug fix, or enhancement, use the `{{slug}}-feature` skill. Simple questions or
single-file clarifications don't need the agent team.

| Agent | Model | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| `{{analyst}}` | {{high tier}} | Research before building; go/no-go memo. Never edits code |
| `{{builder-a}}` | {{low tier}} | {{owned trees}} |
| `{{builder-b}}` | {{low tier}} | {{owned trees}} |
| `{{qa}}` | {{low tier}} | Cross-boundary contract validation. No `Edit` |
| `{{security}}` | {{high tier}} | Audits written code. No `Edit` |

Rules:

- **Routing**: {{path glob}} → `{{agent}}` · {{path glob}} → `{{agent}}`
- **Parallelism**: `{{a}}` ∥ `{{b}}` (disjoint trees). `{{b}}` and `{{c}}` **never in parallel** —
  both write `{{collision file}}`; sequence them or give one a worktree.
- **Model tiering**: {{high}} = research/security/planning; {{low}} = build/QA/verify. Don't
  blanket-upgrade.
- The main thread does research-spawn, gate, and final report only — never inline edits.
- Each agent has memory in `.claude/agent-memory/<agent>/` — read it before re-exploring.
- Intermediate outputs go to `{{scratch dir}}/`; agents return terse receipts + a path.
